{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771215323535,"sessionID":"ses_39b664632ffepC1N1IhxLS7nS2","part":{"id":"prt_c64a821170011KB47Hoo5Jgli2","sessionID":"ses_39b664632ffepC1N1IhxLS7nS2","messageID":"msg_c64a801f2001lpMclh0Af2U2Le","type":"tool","callID":"call_8b29b4e41bc544e8a6a767b8","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find Game component keyboard handlers","prompt":"Find where keyboard event listeners are handled in src/components/Game.tsx. I need to add a handler for the 'KeyG' key code to toggle grid lines. Look for existing keydown event listeners and understand the pattern used.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b57dee5ffeNDT2lefW752DIU (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Keyboard Event Listener Pattern in Game.tsx\n\nI found the keyboard event listener in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx` at **lines 109-121**.\n\n### Current Pattern Used\n\n```typescript\nuseEffect(() => {\n  const handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n    if (e.code === 'Backquote') {\n      e.preventDefault()\n      setSettingsPanelOpen((prev) => !prev)\n    }\n  }\n\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', handleKeyDown)\n  return () => {\n    window.removeEventListener('keydown', handleKeyDown)\n  }\n}, [])\n```\n\n### Pattern Breakdown\n\n1. **Event handler defined inside `useEffect`** - The `handleKeyDown` function is defined within the `useEffect` hook\n2. **Check key code using `e.code`** - Uses the `code` property (not `key`) to check which key was pressed\n3. **`e.preventDefault()`** - Prevents default browser behavior for that key\n4. **State setter with callback** - Uses `(prev) => !prev` pattern for toggling boolean state\n5. **Add/remove event listeners** - Adds listener on mount and removes on cleanup\n\n### Adding the KeyG Handler\n\nGood news! The `showGridLines` state and setter are already available:\n- **State variable**: `showGridLines` (line 45)\n- **State setter**: `setShowGridLines`\n\nYou can modify the existing `handleKeyDown` function to add the KeyG handler:\n\n```typescript\nconst handleKeyDown = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {\n  if (e.code === 'Backquote') {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    setSettingsPanelOpen((prev) => !prev)\n  }\n  if (e.code === 'KeyG') {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    setShowGridLines((prev) => !prev)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe existing onToggleGrid handler (line 452) already toggles this same state, so adding KeyG will work perfectly with the current implementation.\n</task_result>","title":"Find Game component keyboard handlers","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b57dee5ffeNDT2lefW752DIU","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771215266073,"end":1771215323533}}}}
